//! The reference client's own strings, compiled from its vendored English
//! locale.
//!
//! Generated by `tools/gen_text.py` -- do not edit by hand. Run
//! `python tools/gen_text.py` to regenerate, and `--check` to see whether this
//! file is what the tool emits. CI runs the check, so a vendored locale and this
//! table cannot drift apart.
//!
//! Every string the interface shows comes from here. That is the point: the
//! reference is the authority on its own copy, and a sentence retyped by hand
//! is a sentence that drifts. [`Key::name`] is the reference's key verbatim, so
//! a generated name can always be traced back to the file it came from.
//!
//! The strings that carry ICU MessageFormat are compiled into the helper
//! functions below, with the reference's own argument names as their parameters.
//! [`crate::text`] is the runtime they are built from, and says what is
//! deliberately refused rather than approximated.
//!
//! 3846 messages: 353 of them carry ICU markers. Between them they
//! use 80 plurals, 10 selects and 32 grouped
//! numbers, with 56 `#` markers inside plural arms.

#![allow(dead_code)]

